<aside class="border border-warning rounded-box p-4 my-4 space-y-2" aria-label="Before connecting Gmail">
  <p><strong>Before connecting Gmail:</strong> make sure Google Auth Platform → Audience says <strong>In production</strong>. Tokens created while the project is in <strong>Testing</strong> are subject to Google's <strong>7-day</strong> Testing lifetime. Mailsluice cannot check this setting for you.</p>
  <p><strong>Expected Google warning: “Google hasn't verified this app”.</strong> This can appear even after publishing. For your own personal use or a small group of personally known users (fewer than 100 users), Google's <a class="link link-primary" href="https://support.google.com/cloud/answer/13464323" target="_blank" rel="noopener">personal-use exception</a> allows the app to remain unverified.</p>
  <p>When authorizing your own installation, use <strong>Advanced</strong> and the option to continue if Google offers it; the wording may vary. If Google blocks access with no continuation option, check the account or organization's restrictions. Do not switch back to Testing to resolve the warning.</p>
  <p>The unverified-app warning is different from the <a class="link link-primary" href="https://support.google.com/cloud/answer/15549945" target="_blank" rel="noopener">7-day Testing expiration</a>. If you already connected while Testing, first publish the project, then click <strong>Reconnect</strong> once to obtain fresh authorization and preserve your sources.</p>
</aside>
